attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on the anchor and a short spine.** Column 0, `mcbA`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls, and the model names 99% of them {S1}. Then columns 2 to 8, `ybiX` to `dinG`, are carried by 90 to 93%, all persistent, named 92 to 99.6%, fewest at column 5, `ybiE`, 92% {S3}.

@variable **A variable column and a fork break the spine.** Column 1, `fiu`, is variable, carried by 88%, the most plastic stretch of the window {S2.c1, P}. Column 9, `ybiA`, is a fork, carried by 64%, with `espX2` at 13% {S4.c9}. Through columns 41 to 44 a branch of 4 shell families runs in 11 to 14%, [[phage tail assembly]] {S8.b41, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 95 against 87%, and hesitates less there, 0.17 against 0.71 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 35, `ybhC`, a fork column, 1.86 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in the `sdh` genes.** Columns 76 to 79, `sdhB` to `sdhC`, are [[succinate dehydrogenase]] {S8.c76-79, Q}. The last column is `sdhC`, in 26% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 90% of genes**, 0.49 bits on average, perplexity 1.6 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.48 against 0.19 bits, and names fewer genes, 72% against 96% {C}.

